<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 1-wk T-bills 43 pct sold, yield 3.67 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 1-wk T-bills 43 pct sold, yield 3.67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bulgarian Finance Ministry's offer of 5.0 billion levs of one-week discount T-bills was 43.08 percent sold on Monday, yielding 3.67 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3010597006</p>
<p> Par value			  5.0 billion levs</p>
<p> Auction date		     January 13, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 15, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    January 22, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    6,191.4 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		96.16 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    2,153.8 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     96.46 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    3.67 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
